{
 "version": 1,
 "_doc": "Positive allowlist of chain steps a hooks pack def may use (site/packs-hooks.js; docs/PACK_SPEC.md 5.2). A method not listed is rejected with E_PACK_HOOKS_INVALID. The file never widens the runtime: the method must also exist on Pattern.prototype. Review rule: a method is listed only if it is (a) a control or structure method that takes numbers or strings, (b) used by a shipped hooks def or documented in site/data/intellisense/strudel.json, and (c) NOT one that compiles or evaluates text (bbexpr, byteBeatExpression, workletSrc, kabel, ...), speaks, draws or adds DOM nodes or window globals (pianoroll, scope, spectrum, punchcard, draw*, ...), loads samples or URLs, registers methods, logs, touches storage / MIDI / OSC / serial, or takes a function (every, off, jux, sometimes, apply, fmap, bind*, with*). To propose a step: add it here with its args shapes in a PR that also names the shipped def or documented use, and the reviewer applies the rule above. Wire targets: wire's first argument is the control it writes. It must name an entry here with \"wire\": true, a plain value control that takes a number (not s/sound/bank/vowel, not structure or time methods, not wire/hook). Any other target is rejected with E_PACK_HOOKS_INVALID. Review rule for the flag: the entry is a Strudel control (registered in its control/alias registry) whose value is a number. Any argument used as a name (method, property key, param, event) must be validated against a closed set: wire target -> entries flagged wire; $param -> own def params; hook expression -> hook defs at query time.",
 "limits": {
  "str": 256,
  "args": 6,
  "expr": 64
 },
 "shapes": {
  "scalar": "finite number, string (limits.str), boolean or null",
  "param": "{\"$param\": \"<param name>\"} substituted by the hooks engine from the def params",
  "mini": "{\"$mini\": \"<mini-notation string>\"} parsed as mini-notation by the hooks engine, never evaluated as code",
  "wire-opts": "{range?: [a, b], op?: \"<word>\", r?: number}; a and b are numbers or {\"$expr\": \"<arithmetic over params: digits . + - * / ( ) and param names>\"}",
  "groove-opts": "{swing?, push?, jitter?, vel?, drift?, seed?, grid?}: each a finite number or {\"$param\": \"<param name>\"}; the engine (site/engine/groove.js) clamps to the documented range. Declarative: .groove is a pure timing/velocity map of haps, no code runs"
 },
